  "id": "COMPOUND:32420 - PROTEIN:3551",
  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to interact with 3-dehydroquinate dehydratase through a series of molecular targets that are all inhibited by flavopiridol. This suggests a potential pathway where Oblonganoside C acts as a ligand that indirectly targets and inhibits flavopiridol, which in turn affects the activity of 3-dehydroquinate dehydratase. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Oblonganoside C is a broad-acting compound that may influence multiple kinases, including LIM domain kinase 2 and Kappa-casein, all of which are targets of flavopiridol. This implies that the inhibition of these kinases by flavopiridol could lead to the inhibition of 3-dehydroquinate dehydratase, potentially through a common downstream effect. The integration of these findings highlights a possible mechanism where the interaction between Oblonganoside C and flavopiridol leads to the modulation of key metabolic enzymes, suggesting a role in metabolic regulation or disease pathophysiology.",
